## Migrations

Flyway applies `src/main/resources/db/migration/V<n>__<name>.sql` on start, in version order,
and records them in `flyway_schema_history`. Add a new file for every change; never edit an applied one.

Test them against a throwaway database:

```bash
TEST_DATABASE_URL=jdbc:... TEST_DATABASE_USER=... TEST_DATABASE_PASSWORD=... ./mvnw verify
```
{{- end}}

## Logging

Log4j 2 (Logback is excluded) writes JSON with snake_case fields: `@timestamp`, `level`, `message`, `service`, `env`, `request_id`, `logger`.
`RequestIdFilter` puts `request_id` in the ThreadContext for each request and clears it afterwards.
Keep `message` constant and put dynamic values in their own fields:

```java
try (var ctx = CloseableThreadContext.put("order_id", id)) {
    LOG.info("order created");
}
```

Log an error once, at the boundary, with the exception: `LOG.error("payment failed", e);`.
Never log passwords, tokens, API keys or personal data.
